From c423534740278b8c71ba81d15edd0e6069af51dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jetson <jetson@orin-nano.tail52323b.ts.net>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:18:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] nv_attach: by-value fixes after review (one word, line
 forms, decimal fds)

An independent review of 1d95c160 (three lenses; another agent traced each
finding on its input): 14 findings, 13 confirmed, one refuted as a test
remark (taken anyway). None is reachable from llvmbpf's output in the
dumps (lat_mmvq, lat four kernels, carry, carry1), except as noted.

- A 9-16 byte area whose probe writes got two .param return values; a
  device function returns at most one (PTX ISA 7.1.1), so ptxas would
  refuse the module and it would run unprobed. Reachable by ordinary
  output (a 16-byte value, two 8-byte maps). By value is now one word
  (8 bytes); larger areas keep the address form.
- The rewrite works on lines, so text the line scan reads differently from
  the tokenizer now keeps the address form: a block comment, a directive
  glued to a statement (.loc), a guard on a line of its own (it would have
  moved onto the give-back and left the ret unguarded), a kernel probe
  call sharing its line (a trailing branch skipped the write-back; text
  before a guard was repeated).
- A lookup result stored into its own value passed and stored 1.
- Pre-existing, also in the address form: constant_fd read 010 (octal 8)
  as 10 and took a mov out of a comment; it now takes a plain decimal, as
  an immediate or a register's only definition found by statement.
  build_index skipped redux.sync and stacksave as non-writing (prefix
  match on "red" and "st"); it now matches the whole base mnemonic.
- Stats: kernels whose probes never reach the area (no area, nothing
  passed) are counted apart; the log lines say so. Header and trampoline
  comments describe both forms; the header no longer says every map call
  is checked (helpers 1-3 are) or that compares are line-checked.
- Tests: every fallback row asserts its reason; new rows for joined
  lookup results, a result loaded through itself, a 16-byte area, octal
  fds, redux.sync/stacksave, block comments, a lone guard, .loc before a
  ret, an unaligned value, calls sharing a line, a result stored into its
  own value; a fd mov in a comment no longer misleads. 27 routing cases,
  566 assertions.

lat_mmvq's and the four-kernel lat's generated PTX are byte-identical to
1d95c160's (81ea6349...; 64981fbd/ce601e2b/ce6f2d69), so passes t1/t2
stand; fallback tools' PTX (carry, tlatomic, hist, latold) is still
identical to the address-form build's; eight pt_victim tools exact.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
